# Continuous walk and 8-direction keys (owner request 2026-11-08, ROADMAP O434; client/BASE.md "0190"; applies after 0001-0189).
# (1) Creature::walk: a step that starts right after the previous one ended on time starts as far into its animation as it
# is late (at most 40 ms and a third of the step), so one frame or one dispatcher turn of lateness per step no longer
# stretches the walk into stop-go (held key, monster walk packets, auto-walk). A real pause (over 40 ms) or a cancelled
# step carries nothing. (2) Numpad keys keep their numpad key code with NumLock on (X11, Windows), so numpad 1/3/7/9 walk
# the diagonals and 8/4/6/2 straight in either state (they were the number-row codes with NumLock on). (3) game_walking:
# Diagonal movement (Smart Walk) is on by default and switched on once per computer; a walk from standing waits 35 ms for a
# second direction key, so W+D / Up+Right walk the diagonal at once. The diagonal step time (7/5, server patch 0018)
# is unchanged.
