+// Chaos (base-patch 0190): a step that starts right after the previous one ended on time (a held key, the next walk
+// packet of a monster, an auto-walk) starts as far into its animation as it is late, so a frame or a dispatcher turn of
+// lateness no longer stretches every step (a stop-go walk). At most this many ms, and at most a third of the step.
+static constexpr int ChaosWalkCarryMaxTicks = 40;
+
 // Chaos (base-patch 0029, server src-patch 0018 "Movement speed"): the server rounds a player's step up to 10 ms (not the
 // 50 ms beat) and a player's diagonal step takes 7/5 of a straight one (not 3x); monsters and NPCs keep the beat and
 // step diagonally in the time of a straight step (the server's stock diagonal cost of 1.5 is truncated to 1).
